---@class posthog.evaluations.CreateEvaluationRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field name? string Name of the evaluation.
---@field description? string Optional description of what this evaluation checks.
---@field directory_id? string|distilled.Null Directory containing the evaluation. Pass null to move the evaluation to the top level.
---@field enabled? boolean Whether the evaluation runs automatically on new $ai_generation events.
---@field evaluation_type? posthog.evaluations.EvaluationTypeEnum|string 'llm_judge' uses an LLM to score outputs against a prompt; 'hog' runs deterministic Hog code; 'sentiment' classifies user-message sentiment (trained on English, so use 'llm_judge' for multilingual agents). * `llm_judge` - LLM as a judge * `hog` - Hog * `sentiment` - Sentiment analysis
---@field evaluation_config? posthog.evaluations.CreateEvaluationRequestEvaluationConfig Configuration dict. For 'llm_judge': {prompt}; for 'hog': {source}; for 'sentiment': {source: 'user_messages'}.
---@field output_type? posthog.evaluations.OutputTypeEnum|string Output format: 'boolean', 'numeric' for a finite score, 'categorical' for category keys, or 'sentiment' for sentiment analysis. * `boolean` - Boolean (Pass/Fail) * `numeric` - Numeric * `categorical` - Categorical * `sentiment` - Sentiment
---@field output_config? posthog.evaluations.CreateEvaluationRequestOutputConfig Output config. For 'boolean' output_type: {allows_na} to permit N/A results, and {true_is_failure} to declare that a true result means the evaluation found a problem. For boolean decision-model judges, decision_threshold is a probability from 0 to 1 (default 0.5). For 'numeric': only min/max/step, allows_na, and passing_rule {operator: 'gte'|'lte', threshold}. For 'categorical': options [{key, label}], selection_mode (single or multiple), allows_na, and optional passing_rule {categories: [key]}. Do not send true_is_failure for numeric or categorical output. For 'sentiment': {}.
---@field conditions? posthog.evaluations.CreateEvaluationRequestConditionsList Trigger conditions that filter which events are evaluated. OR between condition sets, AND within each. Each set is {id, rollout_percentage, properties[]} — `rollout_percentage` (0-100, defaults to 100) is the sampling field the dispatcher reads.
---@field target? posthog.evaluations.EvaluationTargetEnum|string What the evaluation runs on. 'generation' evaluates each matching $ai_generation event individually. 'trace' evaluates the whole trace once and 'session' the whole $ai_session_id session once: the first matching generation schedules a run that waits for the unit to settle, then evaluates all of its events together. Condition filters still match individual generations — a unit is evaluated when any of its generations matches, and sampling applies per unit. A 'session' evaluation only fires for generations that carry $ai_session_id. When and how the run fires is controlled by target_config's settle strategy. * `generation` - Generation * `trace` - Trace * `session` - Session
---@field target_config? posthog.evaluations.CreateEvaluationRequestTargetConfig Target-specific config. Send {} or omit it for 'generation'. For 'trace' and 'session' targets: a settle config, either 'fixed_window' {window_seconds} or 'inactivity' {quiet_period_seconds, max_age_seconds}. Omit `strategy` to use the target's default. The server fills in any other field you omit, using per-target defaults, and the accepted bounds also depend on `target`.
---@field model_configuration? posthog.evaluations.ModelConfigurationInput|distilled.Null Provider and model for an llm_judge evaluation. Required when creating or switching to llm_judge. To add or replace a model, provide both provider and model. On an existing configured llm_judge, omit this field to keep the current model; null is rejected. When switching an llm_judge to hog or sentiment, set this field to null. Legacy llm_judge evaluations without a model remain editable without adding one. The nested provider_key_id may be null.
---@field deleted? boolean Set to true to soft-delete the evaluation.

