---@class posthog.evaluations.EvaluationEvaluationConfigCase1
---@field source string Hog source code. Return a boolean, finite number, or category keys matching output_type. Categorical single selection accepts one key or a one-item list; multiple selection accepts a list, including []. Return null only for allowed N/A. Output settings determine which boolean counts as a failure.

---@class posthog.evaluations.EvaluationEvaluationConfigCase2
---@field source? posthog.evaluations.EvaluationEvaluationConfigCase2Source Classify sentiment from user messages in the generation input. The classifier is trained on English, so labels are unreliable for other languages; use an 'llm_judge' evaluation for multilingual agents.

---Classify sentiment from user messages in the generation input. The classifier is trained on English, so labels are unreliable for other languages; use an 'llm_judge' evaluation for multilingual agents.
---@alias posthog.evaluations.EvaluationEvaluationConfigCase2Source "user_messages"

---Output config. For 'boolean' output_type: {allows_na} to permit N/A results, and {true_is_failure} to declare that a true result means the evaluation found a problem. For boolean decision-model judges, decision_threshold is a probability from 0 to 1 (default 0.5). For 'numeric': only min/max/step, allows_na, and passing_rule {operator: 'gte'|'lte', threshold}. For 'categorical': options [{key, label}], selection_mode (single or multiple), allows_na, and optional passing_rule {categories: [key]}. Do not send true_is_failure for numeric or categorical output. For 'sentiment': {}.
---@class posthog.evaluations.EvaluationOutputConfig
---@field allows_na? boolean Whether the evaluation can return N/A for non-applicable generations.
---@field true_is_failure? boolean Boolean output only. Omit for numeric, categorical, and sentiment output. Whether a true result means the evaluation found a problem. False (the default) suits pass/fail evaluations, where a true result satisfied the criteria. Set it to true for detector-style evaluations, so a true result is counted and labeled as a fail.
---@field decision_threshold? number|distilled.Null Boolean decision-model judges only. Minimum probability of true required for a true result, inclusive. Omit or set null to use 0.5. Applies to new runs; historical results are unchanged.
---@field min? number|distilled.Null Inclusive minimum numeric score. Omit for no lower bound. Required for numeric decision models.
---@field max? number|distilled.Null Inclusive maximum numeric score. Omit for no upper bound. Required for numeric decision models and must exceed min.
---@field step? number|distilled.Null Optional positive input increment. Does not round evaluation results.
---@field options? posthog.evaluations.EvaluationOutputConfigOptionsList Categorical output options. Keys identify stored results; labels are displayed to users.
---@field selection_mode? posthog.evaluations.EvaluationOutputConfigSelectionMode Select one category or multiple categories. Multiple selection allows an empty result. Defaults to single.
---@field passing_rule? posthog.evaluations.EvaluationOutputConfigPassingRule|distilled.Null Optional numeric or categorical passing rule. Null removes the rule; historical results use the current rule.

---@class posthog.evaluations.EvaluationOutputConfigOptionsItem
---@field key string Stable category key.
---@field label string Category display label.

